  ## API Documentation – Hospitality ERP Suite
#This section documents the available API endpoints currently implemented in the backend.
🔐 Authentication APIs
1. register API
Endpoint: /register/

Method: POST

Fields:
 -name (string),
 -email (Emailstr),
 -password (string),#password should be one uppercase, special charcter and having charcter(8-15)
 -role (string)

Description: Registers a new user with provided credentials.

2. Login API
Endpoint: /login/
Method: POST
Fields:
 -email (string)
 -password(string)
Description: Stores the login entry. (JWT token login implemented here)

3. profile API
Endpoint:/profile/
method: GET
Description: return the profile of user.

4. Manager-only API
Endpoint:/manager-only/
method: GET
Description: There is no access for staff and guest.

5 PUT /bookings/{id}/checkin → Mark check-in

PUT /bookings/{id}/checkout → Mark check-out

🔹 Housekeeping

POST /housekeeping → Add housekeeping task

##implementation

1.Define Models:
Create a User model in models.py with fields: id, username, email,password, and role.
Use SQLAlchemy ORM to map it to the PostgreSQL users table.

2.Create Schemas:

Define Pydantic models in schemas.py for request/response validation:
RegisterRequest → for registration input
LoginRequest → for login input
UserResponse → for returning user data
TokenResponse → for JWT response

3.Database Connection:
Configure PostgreSQL in database.py

4.Implement Authentication Logic:

In auth.py, add functions for:
-Password hashing & verification (passlib)
-JWT token creation & decoding (python-jose)
-User authentication (validate credentials)
-Role-based access control (role_required dependency)
-get_password_hash(password) → store hashed password
-verify_password(plain, hashed) → check login password
-create_access_token(data) → generate JWT
-decode_access_token(token) → verify JWT

5.In main.py, define endpoints:
-POST /register → register new user
-POST /login → login and return JWT
-GET /profile → accessible by user and manager
-GET /manager-only → accessible only by admin

6.Set Up Role-Based Access:
-Use dependency injection (Depends) to secure routes.

7.Connect Everything:
-FastAPI automatically integrates models (models.py), schemas (schemas.py), authentication logic (auth.py), and routes (main.py).
-Database migrations are handled by SQLAlchemy (tables created with Base.metadata.create_all).
